00:16:12,890 --> 00:16:17,230
It's the percentage used in determining if there is a buying or selling imbalance.

229
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:19,650
The common accepted level is 400 as a minimum.

230
00:16:21,590 --> 00:16:25,350
You know, some people I know use 350. Some people I know use 1,000.

231
00:16:26,530 --> 00:16:28,930
It, 400% is a good starting point.

232
00:16:29,110 --> 00:16:31,677
You know, whether you want to be more

233
00:16:31,677 --> 00:16:33,923
selective or more, you know, let a

234
00:16:33,923 --> 00:16:36,169
few more indications, you know, let a

235
00:16:36,169 --> 00:16:43,229
few more imbalances in, it's up to you. Um, but most softwares will allow you to adjust the imbalance trigger in percent.

236
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:49,300
Imbalance volume threshold.

237
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:53,060
Okay. Now, this is one that's unique to the order flows trader.

238
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,660
Um, you're only going to get it with, uh, the order flows trader.

239
00:16:55,780 --> 00:17:00,220
And what it is, it's the minimum traded volume on the bid or offer when there's an imbalance.

240
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:04,196
It's important if you don't want to see imbalances where volume involved

241
00:17:04,196 --> 00:17:06,773
