00:26:51,972 --> 00:26:54,259
usually a market that's going to go sideways.

381
00:26:54,260 --> 00:27:03,100
Passive buyers are buyers who get filled while working a bid.

382
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:08,420
So, you know, there's two types of buyers. There's aggressive buyers and there's passive buyers.

383
00:27:09,180 --> 00:27:17,240
So, passive buyer is somebody that is working a limit order, whereas an aggressive buyer is someone who buys at the market.

384
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:23,860
Imagine that you are trying to buy a car or trying to buy a house.

385
00:27:23,860 --> 00:27:26,174
You have a price you want to pay and you

386
00:27:26,174 --> 00:27:28,719
don't want to budge from that. You're considered a passive buyer.

387
00:27:29,080 --> 00:27:34,420
You're waiting for that person to come down and meet you at your price. You're waiting for the aggressive seller.

388
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:38,800
Passive buyers are at every price level.

389
00:27:39,860 --> 00:27:43,203
When you see big passive buying in the market, you

390
00:27:43,203 --> 00:27:45,543
know, you should pay attention to it.

391
00:27:45,543 --> 00:27:50,558
You know, numbers that really stick out quite strongly. Sometimes they're more obvious than not.

392
00:27:51,020 --> 00:27:54,760
But in a normal, in a bar, you're going to get passive buyers. You're going to get passive sellers.

393
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:59,075
But when you're reading the order flow, you want to read what's

394
00:27:59,075 --> 00:28:00,985
sort of happening around the edges of

395
00:28:00,985 --> 00:28:05,079
the bars. Oftentimes, we'll give you clues as to what's going on in the market.

396
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:09,102
So, passive sellers, again, it's opposite of what

397
00:28:09,102 --> 00:28:13,039
passive buyers are. These are sellers who get filled while working an offer.

398
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:21,160
So, you know, say the market's $18.88 and three-quarters bid offered at $18.89.

399
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:25,840
The people that are trying to sell it at $18.89 are the passive sellers.

400
00:28:26,060 --> 00:28:29,880
They're happy to sit there and wait for people to buy it at their price.

401
00:28:35,780 --> 00:28:43,220
So, the point of control, again, it's oftentimes referred to as commitment of traders or COT.

402
00:28:43,880 --> 00:28:45,689
It's, you know, in order flow context, it

403
00:28:45,689 --> 00:28:47,498
is the price of the bar where the

404
00:28:47,498 --> 00:28:50,438
most volume occurs. It's, you know, going to have the box around it.

405
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:58,760
Positive delta indicates that more volume was bought from the offer.

406
00:28:58,920 --> 00:29:01,440
In other words, aggressive buyers were stronger than aggressive sellers.

407
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:06,144
So, if you have a bar with positive delta, it means net-net

408
00:29:06,144 --> 00:29:08,906
there was more volume traded on the offer,

409
00:29:08,906 --> 00:29:12,359
people buying the offer than people selling into the bid.

410
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:17,780
Again, when the market's moving up, you expect to see positive delta.

411
00:29:18,500 --> 00:29:21,720
On a market that's moving down, you expect to see negative delta.

412
00:29:23,060 --> 00:29:24,380
Now, that's not always the case.

413
00:29:24,980 --> 00:29:28,334
There's times where you have a market that's

414
00:29:28,334 --> 00:29:31,688
sort of going sideways, and you have, you

415
00:29:31,688 --> 00:29:36,299
know, positive deltas and negative deltas, and nobody's really in control.

416
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:42,720
But delta is really very fascinating, I think.

417
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:46,469
You know, I think it's really, as

418
00:29:46,469 --> 00:29:49,378
far as analysis goes, can really tell

419
00:29:49,378 --> 00:29:53,118
you a lot about what's happening in the markets.

420
00:29:54,620 --> 00:29:56,660
So, ratio bonds high.

421
00:29:57,240 --> 00:30:01,536
Okay, again, this is something that only order flows trader

422
00:30:01,536 --> 00:30:04,973
software has, and it's the ratio I use

423
00:30:04,973 --> 00:30:09,699
to determine if there's a small print occurring in a bar.

424
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:12,513
I set my ratio bonds high at 28 because I want to

425
00:30:12,513 --> 00:30:14,112
be notified when there's a ratio above 28,

