00:30:14,112 --> 00:30:17,082
which will indicate there's a small print at the edge of the bar.

427
00:30:18,460 --> 00:30:20,460
I refer to this as small print or single print.

428
00:30:20,540 --> 00:30:23,920
A single print is a volume between 0, sorry, between 1 and 9.

429
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:27,000
A small print will be a volume that's more than 10.

430
00:30:28,780 --> 00:30:30,800
What is important is the ratio number.

431
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:39,120
It indicates a lack of follow-through or, you know, a lack of buying or a lack of selling.

432
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:43,080
It's a reversal indicator in general.

433
00:30:43,900 --> 00:30:45,400
It's this one. It's called ratio bonds high.

434
00:30:46,160 --> 00:30:48,660
And this is the setting.

435
00:30:49,300 --> 00:30:51,740
I'll talk about it a bit more when I get to small prints.

436
00:30:51,740 --> 00:30:56,041
But when I say ratio bonds high, it's a level that I

437
00:30:56,041 --> 00:30:58,908
use to determine if there's going to be

438
00:30:58,908 --> 00:31:05,359
a lack of buying follow-through on a move up or a lack of selling on a move down.

439
00:31:07,520 --> 00:31:14,360
A ratio bonds low is what I use to determine if there's a large print occurring in a bar.

