00:31:29,916 --> 00:31:34,859
be an indication of, you know, strong buying at the bottom of the bar.

445
00:31:35,020 --> 00:31:41,820
If it appears at the top of a red bar, it indicates strong offers up at the top of the bar.

446
00:31:41,820 --> 00:31:49,160
Again, I'll talk about the... Well, I did talk about the ratios of the large print earlier.

447
00:31:49,780 --> 00:31:52,420
And this is what the setting is. It's the ratio bonds low.

448
00:31:52,580 --> 00:31:57,800
Again, it's something that's only available in the OrderFlows trader software.

449
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:07,220
A selling imbalance occurs when sellers are aggressively selling into the bid

450
00:32:07,220 --> 00:32:10,740
at a ratio of 400% or greater relative to what's sold at the bid.

451
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:13,300
So here you've got 769 against 112.

452
00:32:13,300 --> 00:32:16,151
The ratio of, you know, when

453
00:32:16,151 --> 00:32:19,002
the market was 1929.5 bid offered at 1929.75,

454
00:32:19,002 --> 00:32:25,179
769 lots were sold into the bid versus only 112 were bought on the offer.

455
00:32:27,600 --> 00:32:31,000
So that ratio of 112 into 769 is greater than 400.

456
00:32:31,500 --> 00:32:35,020
That's why you have a selling imbalance there.

457
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:44,720
It can help you determine, you know, when sellers are really being aggressive in the market.

458
00:32:44,720 --> 00:32:49,640
Obviously, there's going to be time, you know, everything that's sold into the bid is by aggressive sellers.

459
00:32:49,840 --> 00:32:52,548
But what you want to see is when

460
00:32:52,548 --> 00:32:55,256
the sellers are really being aggressive and you're

461
00:32:55,256 --> 00:32:59,318
stringing together, you know, stacking up, selling imbalances right in a row.

462
00:33:06,570 --> 00:33:11,790
Side-by-side point of control is when the point of control occurs at the same level in two consecutive bars.

463
00:33:12,790 --> 00:33:16,670
You know, here you have one, two, right at the same level, 18.95.

464
00:33:16,670 --> 00:33:20,590
And why is it important?

465
00:33:20,850 --> 00:33:25,610
Well, the volume is in each bar is at the same point.

466
00:33:26,450 --> 00:33:32,590
And, you know, why is that important? Well, it's important because that's where,

467
00:33:32,950 --> 00:33:37,870
that's a price where all, you know, most of the transactions in the bars were occurring.

468
00:33:38,610 --> 00:33:42,990
You know, you can look at it, a lot of people take it to be support or resistance levels.

469
00:33:42,990 --> 00:33:44,526
You know, if the market trades

470
00:33:44,526 --> 00:33:46,062
back up, you know, in this

471
00:33:46,062 --> 00:33:47,598
case, you know, it's, originally this

472
00:33:47,598 --> 00:33:52,208
bar was green and then the bar turned around, it's red, you know, it sold off a bit.

473
00:33:52,270 --> 00:33:53,710
We came back up, around to

474
00:33:53,710 --> 00:33:55,150
the point of control, you know,

475
00:33:55,150 --> 00:33:59,470
got through it a little bit, but then we started staying below it and the market sold off.

476
00:34:00,130 --> 00:34:07,850
You know, point of control is important to determine the support or resistance levels in the market.

477
00:34:10,489 --> 00:34:11,784
Okay, a single

478
00:34:11,784 --> 00:34:13,943
print. Now, a single print

479
00:34:13,943 --> 00:34:16,533
is, again, it's something, well, you

480
00:34:16,533 --> 00:34:19,987
can see it on any order flow chart,

481
00:34:20,310 --> 00:34:22,133
but my software, the order

482
00:34:22,133 --> 00:34:24,686
flows trader software, will put a box

483
00:34:24,686 --> 00:34:29,427
around a single print just to sort of make it stand out more

484
00:34:29,429 --> 00:34:31,730
because, you know, sometimes you're looking at a lot of numbers

485
00:34:31,730 --> 00:34:33,531
and you tend to overlook things, whereas

486
00:34:33,531 --> 00:34:35,590
when you see it, you know, with a

487
00:34:35,590 --> 00:34:37,649
box around it, it just stands out more.

488
00:34:37,650 --> 00:34:41,812
A single print is when there's a volume between one lot and

489
00:34:41,812 --> 00:34:44,587
nine lots at the bottom of a green

490
00:34:44,587 --> 00:34:48,749
candlestick or at the top of a red candlestick here and here.

491
00:34:49,730 --> 00:34:53,050
The setting is ratio bounds high, which I had explained before.

492
00:34:57,880 --> 00:35:04,280
A small print is, small print is when the ratio bounds high prints a ratio number above 28.

493
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:11,140
So, a small print at the edge of a bar

494
00:35:11,140 --> 00:35:12,900
indicates a lack of buyers at the top

495
00:35:12,900 --> 00:35:16,420
of a red candlestick or a lack of sellers at the bottom of a green candlestick.

496
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:18,600
Also see, you know, ratio bounds high.

497
00:35:18,860 --> 00:35:21,104
This one here is actually a ratio bounds

498
00:35:21,104 --> 00:35:23,348
high, indicating that it's just, you know, based

499
00:35:23,348 --> 00:35:25,592
on the volume numbers up here at the

500
00:35:25,592 --> 00:35:29,239
top, there's just a little bit heavier volume that's traded on the top.

501
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:31,840
This one down here,

502
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:37,720
because it has a ratio of 0.4, of 45.06, which indicates a small print.

503
00:35:38,640 --> 00:35:40,400
You know, it's 18 lots traded there.

504
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:42,540
It's a ratio of the numbers involved.

505
00:35:43,180 --> 00:35:46,740
This is also a ratio of the numbers involved, but this is a ratio bounds low.

506
00:35:46,860 --> 00:35:49,100
This is indicating stopping volume.

507
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:54,760
Again, you know, it's a ratio that you're only going to see with the order flows trader.

508
00:35:55,700 --> 00:35:58,660
You know, if you're just looking at this on regular software,

509
00:35:58,720 --> 00:36:00,284
you're not going to know that there's

510
00:36:00,284 --> 00:36:01,401
some, you know, even though

511
00:36:01,401 --> 00:36:03,859
it's kind of hidden in there, it's really hard to see

512
00:36:03,860 --> 00:36:09,820
and these numbers don't look that great, 1962, 245, 29, but it's indicating that there's some stopping volume

513
00:36:09,820 --> 00:36:11,680
and, you know, the market did react off of it.

514
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:15,694
Here you have the small print at the bottom of

515
00:36:15,694 --> 00:36:19,359
this green candlestick, you know, and the market reacted off of it.

516
00:36:20,380 --> 00:36:22,793
When you see a small print, you know,

517
00:36:22,793 --> 00:36:25,206
it's indicating that there was just lack of

518
00:36:25,206 --> 00:36:30,938
selling, you know, when you're at the bottom of this bar and the market turned around and closed higher.

519
00:36:34,590 --> 00:36:41,630
Stacked imbalance, stacked imbalance occurs when there are three or more buying imbalances stacked on top of each other.

520
00:36:42,410 --> 00:36:43,970
That's, you know, hence the term stacked.

521
00:36:44,490 --> 00:36:48,210
So here is a green stacked buying imbalance.

522
00:36:49,210 --> 00:36:52,170
We have the green zone drawn out.

523
00:36:52,250 --> 00:36:54,450
So you got buying imbalance, buying imbalance, buying imbalance.

524
00:36:54,450 --> 00:36:56,890
You know, it's

525
00:36:56,890 --> 00:37:02,750
a form of support or resistance that's generated by market activity.

526
00:37:03,570 --> 00:37:08,110
So when you have a buying imbalance, a stacked buying imbalance and the market trades back in,

527
00:37:08,130 --> 00:37:10,071
you're looking for these buyers to come

528
00:37:10,071 --> 00:37:11,457
back in and reassert themselves

529
00:37:11,457 --> 00:37:14,508
and support the market and for the market to go higher.

530
00:37:16,410 --> 00:37:20,890
A stacked selling imbalance occurs when there are three or more selling imbalances stacked on top of each other.

531
00:37:21,490 --> 00:37:27,010
So in this case, you have, you know, four you know, you got this, the red zone drawn out here

532
00:37:27,010 --> 00:37:34,110
and again, for selling imbalance, stacked selling imbalance, you're going to use it as resistance

533
00:37:34,110 --> 00:37:36,450
whereas a stacked buying imbalance would be support

534
00:37:36,450 --> 00:37:40,930
because you're looking for if the market to trade back up towards where these sellers were earlier

535
00:37:40,930 --> 00:37:45,050
for to these sellers to reappear and sort of push the market back down.

536
00:37:45,770 --> 00:37:46,950
Now, they don't always hold.

537
00:37:47,090 --> 00:37:50,510
Sometimes, you know, these sellers, you know, may just be a big order working its way through the market

538
00:37:50,510 --> 00:37:53,830
and, you know, once they get done, you know, the market comes back up

539
00:37:53,830 --> 00:37:58,930
it's something that, you know, you should take it with the context of what's going on in the market

540
00:37:58,930 --> 00:38:03,770
just because there's a stacked imbalance doesn't necessarily mean that,

541
00:38:03,930 --> 00:38:08,010
you know, the market will be supported or meet resistance.

542
00:38:08,010 --> 00:38:14,030
again, you should read it all into the context of what the market is doing.

543
00:38:14,130 --> 00:38:18,690
If you get a stacked imbalance either buying or selling in the middle of a range,

544
00:38:19,770 --> 00:38:21,790
you know, it's not as important as,

545
00:38:21,790 --> 00:38:23,810
say, a stacked imbalance at the high

546
00:38:23,810 --> 00:38:26,408
of the day or the low of the day.

547
00:38:30,120 --> 00:38:33,920
Stopping volume. Stopping volume is very similar to a large print.

548
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:39,440
It occurs when there's heavy volume at the edge of a candle that turned at that point.

549
00:38:39,980 --> 00:38:44,120
Setting is under ratio bounds low in the order of the trader. And,

550
00:38:44,220 --> 00:38:47,580
so you can see here is, you know, you got up to 1900

551
00:38:47,580 --> 00:38:51,920
and, you know, just about 18, 99, 3 quarters

552
00:38:51,920 --> 00:38:54,080
and there's a ratio of 0.53.

553
00:38:54,260 --> 00:38:57,600
So it's indicating that there's heavy volume up here at the top of this bar

554
00:38:57,600 --> 00:38:59,960
that the market couldn't get past.

555
00:39:00,240 --> 00:39:02,040
And, obviously, the market sold off in this bar

556
00:39:02,040 --> 00:39:05,420
and then continued into the next bar to see a big negative delta appearing.

557
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:07,360
But this was a sign

558
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:09,580
early that, you know, hey, there's some volume.

559
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:12,880
There's some sellers up here at these levels

560
00:39:12,880 --> 00:39:17,340
to, you know, really, you know, put their foot on the,

561
00:39:17,420 --> 00:39:21,040
put their foot on the head of the market and keep it down.

562
00:39:24,540 --> 00:39:25,460
Unfinished business

563
00:39:25,460 --> 00:39:31,880
is when there's volume on both the bid and the offer at the top or the bottom of the candle.

564
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:33,460
It's referred to as unfinished business

565
00:39:33,460 --> 00:39:36,180
as the market often comes back to that level to finish that

566
00:39:36,180 --> 00:39:37,480
business later.

567
00:39:39,580 --> 00:39:41,298
You know, basically, it's an

568
00:39:41,298 --> 00:39:43,016
unfinished auction and, you know,

569
00:39:43,016 --> 00:39:44,734
the thinking behind it is

570
00:39:44,734 --> 00:39:48,858
that, you know, the market will come back and finish that business.

571
00:39:49,300 --> 00:39:53,640
You should have, you know, a zero on the right side of a green candle.

572
00:39:54,060 --> 00:39:55,888
On the left side of a

573
00:39:55,888 --> 00:39:57,716
red candle when it's not, you

574
00:39:57,716 --> 00:40:01,678
know, when you have volume on both sides that's what's considered unfinished business

575
00:40:01,680 --> 00:40:02,640
and you're looking for the market

576
00:40:02,640 --> 00:40:05,560
to come back and finish that business.

577
00:40:05,780 --> 00:40:07,940
You know, like in this case, the market opened up,

578
00:40:08,020 --> 00:40:09,560
you know, down here, traded lower,

579
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:13,360
but then came back and closed that, you know, closed that level off.

580
00:40:13,660 --> 00:40:14,500
Here you have another one,

581
00:40:14,580 --> 00:40:17,120
the market came right back up and so on.

582
00:40:22,620 --> 00:40:26,180
Volume, volume is, everybody should know what volume is.

583
00:40:26,240 --> 00:40:28,280
It's the amount of contracts traded in a bar.

584
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:31,760
There's cumulative volume and there's just volume for the bar.

585
00:40:31,980 --> 00:40:33,700
In this case, I'm talking about volume for the bar.

586
00:40:34,860 --> 00:40:38,120
And so you can see, you know, $34,000, $37,000, $26,000.

587
00:40:39,120 --> 00:40:40,760
You know, it's important because there's going to be times

588
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:43,178
where bars have, you know, very

589
00:40:43,178 --> 00:40:45,596
light volume and, you know, you

590
00:40:45,596 --> 00:40:48,014
want to, you want to understand

591
00:40:48,014 --> 00:40:54,059
that and, you know, take it all into context with what's happening in the market.

592
00:40:58,140 --> 00:41:02,620
The volume imbalance is the difference between the volume traded on the offer and the volume traded on the bid.

593
00:41:03,060 --> 00:41:06,040
When the volume imbalance is over 400%

594
00:41:06,040 --> 00:41:08,220
on the offer side, it's called a buying imbalance.

595
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:13,800
When there's volume imbalance over 400% on the bid side, it's called a selling imbalance.

596
00:41:14,100 --> 00:41:18,660
You know, I had talked about these earlier with a buying imbalance or a selling imbalance.

597
00:41:20,420 --> 00:41:21,760
Here's just the general term.

598
00:41:21,860 --> 00:41:25,700
So you can see all the blue numbers as opposed to the black numbers inside a bar.

599
00:41:26,240 --> 00:41:29,720
If it's a blue number above or below, that's the ratio.

600
00:41:29,980 --> 00:41:31,480
That's the order flows trader ratio.

601
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:39,060
But most software will indicate to you in the footprint where there's a volume imbalance.

602
00:41:41,620 --> 00:41:43,627
It's, you know, when you're starting

603
00:41:43,627 --> 00:41:45,634
to see multiple volume imbalances inside

604
00:41:45,634 --> 00:41:50,318
a bar, it's indicating whether or not the buying or selling is picked up.

605
00:41:57,240 --> 00:41:58,280
The volume profile.

606
00:41:58,720 --> 00:42:03,600
Volume profile shows how much volume is occurred at each price level, throughout the trading session.

607
00:42:03,820 --> 00:42:05,680
It's plotted on the vertical axis of the chart.

608
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:13,820
High volume nodes represent key areas of support and resistance as well as low volume also is, you know,

609
00:42:13,820 --> 00:42:15,660
areas that people look at the markets to go back.

610
00:42:15,740 --> 00:42:18,220
I'm not going to get into volume profile very much in this course.

