00:42:26,020 --> 00:42:31,700
profile trading has been around for a long time, I'll say a long time, you know, 30 years.

613
00:42:32,260 --> 00:42:37,640
But, you know, there's a lot of good information out there on it already.

614
00:42:38,060 --> 00:42:41,200
It's, you know, most people actually already have a basic knowledge of it.

615
00:42:41,760 --> 00:42:43,540
You know, it's something that people look at

616
00:42:43,540 --> 00:42:48,800
that, you know, helps them determine where there's support or resistance in the market.

617
00:42:52,200 --> 00:42:55,480
So, that's the end of lesson four, the order flow terms.

618
00:42:55,580 --> 00:42:57,108
In the next lesson, I'll discuss who

619
00:42:57,108 --> 00:42:58,636
are the market participants and why they

620
00:42:58,636 --> 00:43:01,038
matter and how they determine when they're active in the market.

621
00:43:01,620 --> 00:43:05,140
You want to know when, you know, the big traders are in the market.

622
00:43:05,280 --> 00:43:08,860
You don't necessarily care when, you know, the market's moving on small traders.

623
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:12,620
But, you know, when there's real money

624
00:43:12,620 --> 00:43:20,140
hitting the market, you know, real money accounts coming in and accumulating position or distributing their position, getting out,

625
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:25,720
